      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T15:32:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This ordering seems weird:\n1. What is the difference between EXCESSIVE and DEBUG?\n2. What is MSGDUMP?\n3. Shouldn\u0027t ERROR messages always be reported?  In any case, ERROR and WARNING aren\u0027t debug levels, so they shouldn\u0027t be here.  I think you should remove ERROR and move WARNING to its own enableWarnings(bool enable); method.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f08d07b7_cbc53436",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T18:56:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The HIDL interface for wpa_supplicant is a wrapper over the existing control interfaces exposed by wpa_supplicant. The ordering of this and most other parameters in these \nhidl interfaces mirror the existing internal values exposed by wpa_supplicant: https://cs.corp.google.com/android/external/wpa_supplicant_8/src/utils/wpa_debug.h?rcl\u003d370387c3707c1577dc33e4d6b2bb19f459325222\u0026l\u003d22.\n\nWe had a discussion regarding this in b/31646498. I\u0027m trying to avoid boilerplate code for things that will probably never be changed.",
      "parentUuid": "f08d07b7_9adffc23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
