    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f08d07b7_bab598e9",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000866
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T15:32:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How is this information retrieved by the framework?  The driver is a low-level concept, and is potentially something the framework should not be worried about.  Is this what tied into the IWiFi interface?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f08d07b7_700fb1e7",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T18:56:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. I think we can get rid of this in the HIDL interface. \nThis is a generic interface exposed by wpa_supplicant to support multiple platforms. But, on android this will always be \"nl80211\" and I don\u0027t think any of the vendors configure this parameter in any other way.",
      "parentUuid": "f08d07b7_bab598e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f08d07b7_daa264b1",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000866
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T15:32:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Configuration files in HIDL must be self-describable, so this needs to be converted to XML with its own schema that is then checked in with the interface as well.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f08d07b7_b08e992f",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T18:56:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "wpa_supplicant.conf is a custom file used by wpa_supplicant. We cannot change the format of this file. This will not be accepted upstream. \n\nWe\u0027ve been using the wpa_supplicant.conf file (controlled by wpa_supplicant) to persist all the wifi network configurations till now. For O, we\u0027ve now changed this to a new file (b/28966377) controlled directly by framework. \n\nSo, we\u0027re going to get rid of this eventually. b/29352330 is tracking this work item. However, we still need to handle the migration of network configuration data from existing devices.",
      "parentUuid": "f08d07b7_daa264b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5b2a710_0351ad62",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-27T16:55:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you put this in a comment? Can you mirror the conf in an xml file and convert between them?",
      "parentUuid": "f08d07b7_b08e992f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5b2a710_031e4d24",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicant.hal",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-27T17:30:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, we had an internal discussion and decided to take this file out of the HIDL interface. \nThis an implementation detail that should not be a part of the HIDL interface. This file will still be used in most of the HIDL implementations of wpa_supplicant. But, there is no need for this to be specified in the interface by framework.",
      "parentUuid": "e5b2a710_0351ad62",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 22
