      "writtenOn": "2016-09-23T18:56:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Within wpa_supplicant internally, ifaces are uniquely identified by the |ifName| and networks are uniquely identified by |networkId|. \n\nSo, every |ISupplicantNetwork| needs to stor/expose the corresponding |networkId| allocated to the network by wpa_supplicant core.\nEven if we pass the |ISupplicantNetwork| object in |removeNetwork|, we will still need to retrieve the |networkId| of the object to remove it from wpa_supplicant core using |ISupplicantNetwork.getId()|. So, we cannot totally get rid of |SupplicantNetworkId|.",
      "parentUuid": "f08d07b7_15973f3a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "d16970d89ecbaecdb4c210d8ed1b3aef9a16e071",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
